WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:04.467
It was a sunny morning in Prickly Pear.

2
00:00:04.468 --> 00:00:09.274
The town's sheriff was already hard at work, studying a local map.

3
00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:14.369
Meanwhile his deputy was sound asleep.

4
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.307
"There's a lot of land around this town."

5
00:00:17.308 --> 00:00:20.198
Roscoe took a sip of tea.

6
00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:25.228
"Plenty of places for outlaws to hide."

7
00:00:25.229 --> 00:00:28.796
"Zzz . . . Zzz . . ."

8
00:00:28.797 --> 00:00:33.741
"Cleo!" Roscoe frowned. "Wake up!"

9
00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:37.369
Cleo opened one eye.

10
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.174
"I'm saving my energy for later."

11
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:44.695
Just then Mayor Wayne rushed in with Oswald.

12
00:00:44.696 --> 00:00:47.774
"Sheriff! Deputy!" the mayor said.

13
00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:50.164
"Miss Annie is missing!"

14
00:00:50.165 --> 00:00:54.775
Cleo sat up. "Missing?"

15
00:00:54.776 --> 00:00:59.316
Roscoe spilled his tea. "Since when?"

16
00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:03.914
He sure hoped that pretty schoolteacher wasn't in trouble! "She

17
00:01:03.915 --> 00:01:07.945
went to Jerome yesterday with her paints," the mayor said. "She

18
00:01:07.946 --> 00:01:10.295
didn't come back." Oswald's

19
00:01:10.296 --> 00:01:16.380
eyes filled with tears. "You have to find her!" "Don't

20
00:01:16.381 --> 00:01:20.974
worry, kid," Cleo said. "We will." Roscoe

21
00:01:20.975 --> 00:01:25.480
looked at the map again. "Where's Jerome?" "Right

22
00:01:25.481 --> 00:01:29.299
here." Mayor Wayne pointed to it. "It

23
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.429
used to be a busy town. But

24
00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:33.759
it became dangerous. Outlaws

25
00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.226
had slingshot fights right on Main Street. Now

26
00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:40.377
it's just a ghost town." Roscoe's

27
00:01:40.378 --> 00:01:45.342
eyes went wide. "A ghost town?" "It

28
00:01:45.343 --> 00:01:49.961
just means nobody lives there now," Oswald said. Cleo

29
00:01:49.962 --> 00:01:53.402
chuckled. "Silly Roscoe! There

30
00:01:53.403 --> 00:01:57.368
aren't real ghosts in a ghost town." "Well

31
00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:03.477
. . ." Mayor Wayne laughed nervously. "It's

32
00:02:03.478 --> 00:02:05.414
a good name for Jerome. Strange

33
00:02:05.415 --> 00:02:07.948
things happen there. I

34
00:02:07.949 --> 00:02:18.004
don't know if it's haunted, but . . ." He whispered, "Be careful!" ***

35
00:02:18.005 --> 00:02:23.098
The two law officers got their horses and headed to Jerome.

36
00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:26.526
One of them sure was in a hurry!

37
00:02:26.527 --> 00:02:30.522
Cleo tried to keep up with Roscoe.

38
00:02:30.523 --> 00:02:33.996
"You're going too fast!"

39
00:02:33.997 --> 00:02:37.460
Roscoe slowed down.

40
00:02:37.461 --> 00:02:40.654
"You seem worried," Cleo said.

41
00:02:40.655 --> 00:02:45.015
"You really like Annie, don't you?"

42
00:02:45.016 --> 00:02:49.968
"Of course not!" Roscoe pretended to laugh.

43
00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.677
"I mean, I like her. But it's not what you think.

44
00:02:52.678 --> 00:02:56.222
I, um, like lots of folks."

45
00:02:56.223 --> 00:02:59.701
Cleo gave him a funny look. "Stop

46
00:02:59.702 --> 00:03:07.778
looking at me!" Roscoe frowned and sped off again. ***

47
00:03:07.779 --> 00:03:12.560
In Jerome, Main Street was empty and quiet.

48
00:03:12.561 --> 00:03:17.825
Wildflowers grew between the boards of a boardwalk.

49
00:03:17.826 --> 00:03:20.783
"Look! Annie was here."

50
00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:24.893
Cleo pointed to a half-finished painting on an easel.

51
00:03:24.894 --> 00:03:28.417
A blank canvas sat next to it.

52
00:03:28.418 --> 00:03:33.198
A horse grazed on weeds nearby.

53
00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:35.888
Roscoe bit his lip.

54
00:03:35.889 --> 00:03:40.486
"What happened to her?" Cleo looked around.

55
00:03:40.487 --> 00:03:41.833
"I don't know."

56
00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:48.136
Roscoe cupped his paws and shouted, "Miss Annie! Are you here?"

57
00:03:48.137 --> 00:03:51.155
There was no answer.

58
00:03:51.156 --> 00:03:59.073
They got off their horses and tied them to a post.

59
00:03:59.074 --> 00:04:04.185
Fwap! Fwap! Suddenly they heard a slingshot.

60
00:04:04.186 --> 00:04:11.961
Roscoe gasped. "Someone’s attacking us!"

